{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "349437965",
    "title": "SFCC MRT API Capabilities: Spike Findings (SFCC-122)",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/349437965",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 19,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "> SFCC-122 spike deliverable: a documented inventory of the SFCC APIs available through MRT for product, category, and pricing consumption, and what can be built and tested in the lower environments before the AP21/MuleSoft feed is ready.\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| Jira | SFCC-122 (Spike, Squad-A; epic SFCC-1 Platform Setup) |\n| Author | Angelo Navarro, Squad-A / FED Lead |\n| Status | Approved by @Manikandan Ramachandran |\n| Verified against | dev sandbox `bkzk-002`, local PWA run, 23-24 Jul 2026 |\n\n---\n\n1. Summary\n----------\n\n* **What \"MRT API\" means here.** Managed Runtime is the PWA Kit hosting/proxy layer. Product, category, and pricing data are served by **SCAPI (Salesforce Commerce API, the Shopper APIs)**, reached through the MRT proxy (`/mobify/proxy/api`). The separate Managed Runtime Admin API is platform / CI-CD and out of scope.\n* **The APIs are ready; data was the gap.** SCAPI can serve product, category, and pricing today. At spike outset the sandbox had no data because the AP21-to-SFCC feed is not built yet.\n* **Dev is now seeded and verified.**`bkzk-002` has categories, pricebooks, inventory, and manually-created sample products with varied configurations (priced, in stock, with a working promotion strikethrough), all consumable via SCAPI with no app-code change.\n* **Interim data is manual; scale and real data need AP21.** The current sample set was hand-created in Business Manager and continues to be added manually; full-catalogue and real data depend on the permanent AP21 data feed to SFCC (SFCC-121).\n\n---\n\n2. MRT API inventory (Task 1)\n-----------------------------\n\nThe storefront consumes SFCC through the MRT proxy path `/mobify/proxy/api`, base host `{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com` (Dev: shortCode `qmyt7hks`, org `f_ecom_bkzk_002`, site `ZimmermannAU`). Authentication is **SLAS private-client** (guest and registered tokens; the client secret is held server-side). Requests and responses are JSON over TLS.\n\nAPIs relevant to product, category, and pricing:\n\n| API family | Path root | Data served | Verbs | Auth |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Shopper Products | `/product/shopper-products/v1/*` | Product detail (master/variant, images), **price** (`priceRanges` per pricebook), and the **category tree** (`getCategory`) | GET | SLAS |\n| Shopper Search | `/search/shopper-search/v1/*` | Category product listing (`cgid` refinement), keyword search, faceting, sort | GET | SLAS |\n| Shopper Login (SLAS) | `/shopper/auth/v1/*` (`oauth2` token and JWKS) | Guest and registered auth; the enabler for every read above | GET, POST | n/a |\n\n**Payload conventions.** The storefront pulls related data in one call with `expand` (e.g. `expand=prices,promotions,variations,images`) and `perPricebook=true` for pricebook-aware pricing. Promotions surface as `productPromotions` (a `calloutMsg`, and a `promotionalPrice` at the variant level).\n\n**Out of scope** (other problems, documented elsewhere): cart and checkout (Shopper Baskets, Shopper Orders), account and wishlist (Shopper Customers), personalization (Shopper Context, Einstein), OCAPI (configured but not called by app code), MuleSoft direct reads, and the Managed Runtime Admin API.\n\n---\n\n3. What can serve product, category, and pricing now (Task 2)\n-------------------------------------------------------------\n\nVerified by a local PWA run against dev `bkzk-002` (23-24 Jul 2026), SCAPI network traffic captured:\n\n| Capability | API | Verified result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Category tree | Shopper Products `getCategory` | `clothing` and `new-arrivals` return 200; navigable |\n| Category listing / search | Shopper Search | `product-search?refine=cgid=<category>` returns 200 with product hits |\n| Product detail | Shopper Products | `4673TS251` returns 200 with attributes, images, variants |\n| Price | Shopper Products (`expand=prices`, `perPricebook`) | 625 AUD from pricebook `au-aud-list-prices` |\n| Discount / strikethrough | promotions via `expand=promotions` | 10% promo returns `promotionalPrice` 562.50 at variant level; PDP renders A$562.50 against a struck A$625 |\n| Inventory | on the product record | `inventory_m_au`, ats 10, orderable |\n| Auth | SLAS | guest token issued and accepted |\n\n**Conclusion:** SCAPI serves product, category, pricing, and promotional pricing in dev today, and the storefront renders them with **no code change**. Consumption is not the blocker.\n\n---\n\n4. Current data state and how it is populated\n---------------------------------------------\n\n* **Dev** `bkzk-002`**.** Categories, pricebooks, and inventory are configured; a manually-created set of sample products with varied configurations is present, priced and in stock with a working promotion. Business Manager first-time setup (storefront-catalogue assignment, search-index rebuild) is done. IDs in use: master catalogue `zimmermann-catalog`, storefront catalogues `zimmermann-<site>-storefront-catalog`, pricebooks `{site}-{currency}-list-prices` (e.g. `au-aud-list-prices`), inventory list `inventory_m_au`.\n* **Interim (now).** Sample data is **created manually in Business Manager** by platform, because there is no AP21-to-SFCC integration yet. Additional sample data is also manual.\n* **Permanent.** Product and catalogue land via the **AP21 to MuleSoft to SFCC** feed. Price lands as file-based **Pricebook XML from AP21** (there is no pricebook write API, so price is always file-based); the exact delivery path (SFTP, API, or MuleSoft) is not yet confirmed (TSD Price, open item). Building this feed is SFCC-121's scope.\n\n*Loading-mechanism sources: Confluence Business Manager Configuration Management (309657601) and the Catalogue Sync pages (312508418, 315490342). Whether a documented* `data/sample` *bulk-import set exists for the sandbox is unconfirmed (open item).*\n\n---\n\n5. Limitations and gaps (Task 3)\n--------------------------------\n\nTo be covered by AP21/MuleSoft (SFCC-121) or platform:\n\n* **Data breadth.** The dev seed is a manually-created sample set, not the full catalogue, so it is not yet at production scale for faceting or large-listing tests. Filling it out remains manual until the feed exists.\n* **Product attributes not final.** The attribute model is still under discussion (per Victor); attribute-bound PDP/PLP work may need rework.\n* **Sale-pricebook path unexercised.** Discount display is verified via a **promotion**; the sale-pricebook (\"was/now\") path is a separate mechanism and has not been tested. (The sale strategy, promotion vs sale pricebook, is itself an open item in TSD Price.)\n* **Other sites and tiers unconfirmed.** Only `ZimmermannAU` on dev is verified; other storefronts and non-dev tiers are not checked.\n* **Permanent feed pending.** The AP21 data feed to SFCC is not built; SFCC-121 (Validate MuleSoft Sync Process) is In Progress.\n\n---\n\n6. Permanent vs workaround (Task 4)\n-----------------------------------\n\n| Element | Classification |\n| --- | --- |\n| SCAPI-via-MRT for product/category/pricing consumption | **Permanent** (the storefront's supported model; no code change needed) |\n| SLAS private-client auth via MRT | **Permanent** |\n| AP21 data feed to SFCC (catalogue via MuleSoft; price as file-based Pricebook XML, delivery path TBC) | **Permanent** (data population; not yet built) |\n| Manual Business Manager creation of sample data | **Workaround** (interim only; throwaway once the feed delivers) |\n| OCAPI via MRT | Configured fallback; currently unused |\n\n---\n\nReferences\n----------\n\n* Codebase (`zimmermann-pwa`): `.docs/integration/01-sfcc.md`, `03-mulesoft.md`; `config/default.js`; `overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx`, `.../components/_app-config/index.tsx`, `.../ssr.js`, `.../ssr/slasTokens.ts`.\n* Confluence (space SFCC): Business Manager Configuration Management (309657601); Catalogue Sync (312508418, 315490342); TSD Product (292061208); TSD Price (292388871); Technical Solution Design, PWA (256835585).\n* Jira (project SFCC): SFCC-122, SFCC-121 (Validate MuleSoft Sync Process), SFCC-1 (Platform Setup & Environments).\n* Verification: local PWA run against dev `bkzk-002`, SCAPI network capture, 23-24 Jul 2026.\n* Victor Crisostomo: sandbox and follow-up answers (23-24 Jul 2026).\n\n---\n\nChangelog\n---------\n\n* 27 Jul 2026: Reshaped from the earlier TSD-formatted draft into a spike findings / inventory doc, per review feedback (a spike needs findings, not a problem/options/decision TSD; removed PWA-implementation detail that overlapped the PWA TSD). Audited against codebase, Confluence, and JIRA: corrected the SLAS endpoint path, the SFCC-121 status, and the price-feed delivery framing. Refreshed the dev data-state description to reflect an expanded manual sample set with varied configurations. Removed the Open Items section (its points are already covered under Limitations and gaps).\n* Earlier history: TSD-format versions v0.1 to v0.5 (22 to 24 Jul 2026).",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4cb",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

